From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: acqxi <kacqxi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:27:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] Customized build: title marker, restart controls and
 WSL runtime status
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Window titles end with " (Customized)" and Settings > About shows
"(Customized)" next to the version, so this build is never mistaken for
a stock install. Titles only: productName, appId, AppUserModelId, the
userData path and updates keep the stock names.

Settings > About gets a Restart group:
- Reload window reloads only the renderer; backends and turns go on.
- Restart T3 Code stops every backend the normal way and relaunches.
- Hard restart gives backends 3 s, then kills each one's process tree
  (taskkill /T /F on Windows, SIGKILL elsewhere) and, for a WSL backend
  on a staged runtime, every process in the distro running from that
  exact runtime directory with its descendants (wsl.exe -e sh -c with
  the directory as a positional argument, 5 s timeout, best effort),
  then relaunches.
Both restarts ask first. A plain browser shows only Reload window.

On Windows, when T3CODE_CUSTOMIZE_RELAUNCH names an existing launch.ps1,
a relaunch starts that launcher (hidden, -WaitPid <main pid>) and quits
instead of calling app.relaunch, so a rebuilt build opens next time.

The WSL backend reports how its runtime is coming up: the preflight
records probing, installing and starting, and a read-only
desktop:get-wsl-runtime-status joins that with the backend instance
(waiting for readiness, ready, failed). Settings shows it under the WSL
backend row ("Installing runtime · 1m 12s" with an activity bar, then
"Running · runtime sha256-a95e31… · v0.1.12"), and the environments map
shows it on the WSL card and in its detail panel. The page polls every
second while the runtime comes up and every 10 s otherwise. A failed
start offers Retry, which re-runs the existing WSL reconcile, or points
to Restart in wsl-only mode.
